<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ's Anderton rejects NZ-Aust investment talks.</title>
<headline>NZ's Anderton rejects NZ-Aust investment talks.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand Alliance leader Jim Anderton on Wednesday said any agreement allowing Australian investment into New Zealand with &quot;minimum constraint&quot; would be disregarded by an Alliance government.</p>
<p>Anderton said proposed foreign investment would have to satisfy stregthened national interest criteria under the left-wing Alliance.</p>
<p>&quot;The Alliance will not allow Australians or any other overseas investor to buy up our land,&quot; Anderton said.</p>
</text>
